@SYSTEM_TITLE
; `~` is bitwise NOT ("ビットごとの否定"), distinct from `!` which is logical
; NOT ("論理否定") — docs/research/emuera-wiki/exop.md. They used to share
; one AST node (`UnaryOperator::Not`), which broke the common
; `CFLAG &= ~1pN` bitmask-clear idiom by zeroing the whole flag word.
A = 1P4 + 1P2 + 1P0
PRINTFORML {A}

; Clear only bit 2 (value 4) via the bitmask-clear idiom.
A = A & ~1P2
PRINTFORML {A}

; Logical NOT is unaffected by the split: 0 -> 1, nonzero -> 0.
PRINTFORML {!0} {!5}
